1
00:00:01,894 --> 00:00:04,734
Hello, everyone, I'm Tayoni.

2
00:00:05,181 --> 00:00:09,903
Today is Thursday, November 10, 2022,

3
00:00:10,519 --> 00:00:13,976
and I am going to record the 23rd podcast.

4
00:00:14,742 --> 00:00:17,178
How have you all been?

5
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:25,592
After I uploaded the last video, I went to see my sister's family in the US.

6
00:00:26,358 --> 00:00:31,912
In fact, it's already been a week since I came back from America.

7
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:36,799
In the meantime, I've been to the US, but at the same time,

8
00:00:37,331 --> 00:00:45,807
I've also been thinking a lot about my future career after finishing my master's programme recently.

9
00:00:46,623 --> 00:00:50,187
And so much time has passed!

10
00:00:51,251 --> 00:01:00,328
Before recording a new podcast today, I took another look at the comments on recent videos.

11
00:01:01,009 --> 00:01:06,000
First of all, in the previous podcast, the 22nd podcast,

12
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:12,229
I introduced the subscribers' experiences of studying Korean.

13
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:18,722
However, some people could not see the community posts posted before.

14
00:01:19,782 --> 00:01:23,362
So, with the comments added to the video,

15
00:01:23,681 --> 00:01:31,152
I'm going to make a video with a similar theme to that one again next time.

16
00:01:31,526 --> 00:01:41,491
So, if you wanted to leave a comment, but couldn't, please leave a comment on the previous podcast video.

17
00:01:41,618 --> 00:01:45,586
I will make a video like that again.

18
00:01:47,203 --> 00:01:55,127
And for the first time, I took a video of myself talking in front of the camera,

19
00:01:55,596 --> 00:01:58,521
which was a video of making an apple crumble.

20
00:01:59,075 --> 00:02:09,234
To be honest, I felt unsure when uploading it, but I'm really glad that you guys left a lot of good comments.

21
00:02:10,426 --> 00:02:15,351
There are so many oats left now that I bought as an ingredient back then.

22
00:02:15,351 --> 00:02:23,234
So, in the next vlog, I will try to cook something that I can use leftover oats.

23
00:02:25,532 --> 00:02:30,585
And again, there's something new I've tried in the meantime.

24
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:38,425
I've made my voice be heard in places other than YouTube.

25
00:02:39,234 --> 00:02:47,141
If you search for my channel name ‘Tayoni’ on Spotify, Amazon Music, and Apple Podcasts now,

26
00:02:47,545 --> 00:02:52,662
you can probably listen to the sixth episode now.

27
00:02:53,662 --> 00:02:58,857
Actually, in the early days of when I started YouTube,

28
00:02:59,176 --> 00:03:03,189
many people made this request in the comments.

29
00:03:03,593 --> 00:03:08,940
But I didn't know how to do it back then, so I just put it off.

30
00:03:09,876 --> 00:03:16,397
So I spend a day searching for it on the Internet.

31
00:03:16,652 --> 00:03:22,942
Then, I uploaded the podcasts to other platforms.

32
00:03:24,091 --> 00:03:36,288
After uploading like that, the locations where you are listening to my podcasts are displayed on the world map,

33
00:03:36,948 --> 00:03:45,438
which is really interesting to see that my voice is heard from all over the world.

34
00:03:46,246 --> 00:03:54,156
Anyway, as I mentioned, I went to the US for a week,

35
00:03:54,518 --> 00:04:00,415
and today I'd like to talk about this short trip.

36
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:14,074
If you're following my Instagram, you've probably already seen this.

37
00:04:14,744 --> 00:04:23,243
I went to my sister's house in Texas, USA for a week at the end of October.

38
00:04:24,179 --> 00:04:34,482
In fact, she's been living in Texas for quite some time now, but this was the first time I'd actually been to her house.

39
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:42,930
We had met in the US before, but we had travelled to other cities.

40
00:04:43,653 --> 00:04:55,159
But this time, I went straight to Texas because I was going to see a nephew and a niece I had never met in person.

41
00:04:56,308 --> 00:05:02,924
My sister gave birth to her first child just when the covid just started,

42
00:05:03,349 --> 00:05:05,955
and not long ago she gave birth to her second.

43
00:05:06,551 --> 00:05:11,180
Actually, I really wanted to go see her first child before.

44
00:05:11,669 --> 00:05:14,846
But there were a lot of travel restrictions because of the covid,

45
00:05:15,102 --> 00:05:22,571
and I was busy with various things during my master's degree, so I couldn't easily go there.

46
00:05:23,209 --> 00:05:27,326
So, after submitting my master's dissertation on September 1st,

47
00:05:27,985 --> 00:05:33,336
the thing I wanted to do most was to go to Texas and see my sister.

48
00:05:33,868 --> 00:05:39,793
So, as soon as I finished it, I immediately booked a plane ticket.

49
00:05:40,708 --> 00:05:47,187
And, after packing presents for my sister, brother-in-law, niece and nephew,

50
00:05:47,761 --> 00:05:52,410
I finally boarded the plane to Texas on October 24th.

51
00:05:55,580 --> 00:06:02,627
I will never forget how I felt when I saw my niece and nephew for the first time.

52
00:06:03,542 --> 00:06:10,681
The children I only saw on my phone screen were at my sister's house!

53
00:06:11,021 --> 00:06:21,770
And they were a little smaller, cuter and prettier than in the video or photo.

54
00:06:22,345 --> 00:06:29,641
To be honest, when we first met, I was a little worried that they might feel unfamiliar with me,

55
00:06:29,641 --> 00:06:32,439
but we became close to each other really quickly than I thought.

56
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:40,000
So while I was in the US, I read a lot of books, did a lot of crafts together,

57
00:06:40,606 --> 00:06:44,914
played as much as possible and tried to spend time.

58
00:06:45,531 --> 00:06:49,392
I went to pick her up at the kindergarten she attends,

59
00:06:49,542 --> 00:06:55,000
went to the kindergarten Halloween party, and went on a picnic in the park.

60
00:06:55,918 --> 00:07:03,837
It was so cute to see her running to me while calling me “이모”,

61
00:07:04,241 --> 00:07:09,400
which made me feel really sad to see time passing every day.

62
00:07:10,528 --> 00:07:17,708
The second child is a newborn baby who had just turned 100 days, so we couldn't play together,

63
00:07:18,304 --> 00:07:23,995
but I fed him, soothed him when crying, and put him to sleep.

64
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:31,091
It was my first time doing anything like that, which was amazing.

65
00:07:31,793 --> 00:07:44,207
And I felt that it was awesome that my sister has been doing all this with little help from our family.

66
00:07:45,142 --> 00:07:48,918
Actually, I saw her after three and a half years.

67
00:07:49,365 --> 00:07:58,876
So she went through these big events, her pregnancy and childbirth twice, in a period we hadn't seen.

68
00:08:01,068 --> 00:08:07,660
It was a pity that I couldn't be with her during the process due to the covid situation,

69
00:08:08,205 --> 00:08:11,705
but it should get a little easier in the future,

70
00:08:12,343 --> 00:08:18,800
so I think it would be really good if we could meet more often as her children grow up.

71
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,436
Now, I think we should make a promise for next time.

72
00:08:26,968 --> 00:08:33,574
After my short trip to the US, I returned to the UK.

73
00:08:34,425 --> 00:08:41,230
For the first few days after coming back, I think it was a little difficult because I couldn't get used to the jet lag.

74
00:08:41,815 --> 00:08:47,158
Even British daylight saving has just ended, so the time of sunset is getting earlier,

75
00:08:47,434 --> 00:08:51,335
and the temperature has dropped slightly.

76
00:08:52,622 --> 00:08:55,973
So the mood has turned a bit gloomier(?).

77
00:08:56,718 --> 00:09:02,739
So, to lift up the mood again, I made a Christmas wreath,

78
00:09:03,142 --> 00:09:08,366
and I am trying to take as many walks as possible every day.

79
00:09:08,834 --> 00:09:14,674
And at the same time, I am thinking a lot about my future.

80
00:09:15,184 --> 00:09:17,407
Nothing has been decided yet,

81
00:09:17,663 --> 00:09:22,205
but I'm going to spend this period well so that I don't leave any regrets.

82
00:09:23,215 --> 00:09:25,864
How are you all doing?

83
00:09:26,694 --> 00:09:32,805
There must be many people like me who live in places where the weather is getting colder.

84
00:09:33,209 --> 00:09:39,666
I hope you don't shrink in the cold weather and have a lively day.

85
00:09:40,347 --> 00:09:46,400
So, everyone, thank you very much for listening to my podcast today,

86
00:09:46,868 --> 00:09:52,857
and I will come back with another video.

87
00:09:53,538 --> 00:09:56,463
Thank you, everyone. Good-bye!
